A||||1||rodmcneill||Newer headlights on older cars?||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||12-31-2000||01:58 AM||||If I decide to upgrade my 86 headlights to the 87-88 lights do I just need the headlight assm. only? Are these a direct plug in? Same connectors? Do the newer headlights use the old relays or do I need to get the module box also for these newer lights?||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-31-2000||02:43 AM||||You can easily upgrade to the newer (and quieter) '87-'88 headlight motors, but it is more involved than just swapping motor assemblies.  <P>You will need to remove/replace the wiring harness under the hood, bolt on the module to the left front outer headlight bucket (may have to tap a couple of small holes) and install the new motors to the headlight assemblies.<P>The hardest part is removing/installing the harness.  You will need to remove the upper radiator support bracket to get enough clearance.  It really isn't too hard, but you will need to make sure everything is routed correctly.<P>I have a complete "kit" for sale for $100 + shipping.  It includes everything needed to retrofit an '84-'86 Fiero.  For $10 more I will install new drive pins (from Rodney Dickman).<P>LMK if you are interested. ||||reg||1
